  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">POVERTY MONITORING, EVALUATION AND POLICY DESIGN</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The grant (TF050333) will assist creating and institutionalizing reliable and sustainable poverty monitoring, evaluation and policy design mechanisms based on Living Standards Measurement Survey (LSMS) for the timely production of reliable and useful statistical information to assist policy-makers in the design, implementation and evaluation of economic and social programs and spending.  It also aims at developing analytical capacity within the Government to fully utilize the information generation for analysis of poverty issues, monitoring and evaluation of poverty impacts and pro-active poverty reduction policy design.  Finally, it aims at supporting the institution-building process by assigning specific institutional responsibilities and by strengthening the governments technical and managerial capability for targeting and evaluation of social programs and spending and for monitoring of poverty on a regular basis, including ex-ante assessment of poverty, income distributions and social dimensions of all Government decisions and programs.</narrative>
  </description>
